**SONICVEIL — Acoustic Parasite Inverter**  
**BEKW-CODE Open Hardware Spec · Draft v0.1**

**CORE INVERSION**  
Loud noise is currently treated as pure waste and damage. Data-center fans, subway tunnels, lawnmowers, generators, HVAC arrays — all of them scream energy into the air while also cooking the people nearby and (in the data-center case) guzzling water for cooling. We do not silence. We do not complain. We put a mouth on the scream and make it pay rent.

**WHAT IT IS**  
A modular, conformal acoustic skin that does three jobs at once:

1. Piezoelectric + electromagnetic hybrid harvesting of broadband noise (especially the ugly mid-to-high frequency bands that destroy hearing).  
2. Passive and active sound dampening so the residual noise drops below damage thresholds.  
3. Waste-heat and residual vibration capture so the same surface also feeds a secondary low-grade thermal/piezo stream.

Primary target geometries:  
- Data-center exterior wall and roof panels (the constant 40–80 Hz hum + fan scream).  
- Subway tunnel liners and station ceilings.  
- Retrofit muffler sleeves for outdoor power equipment (lawnmowers, leaf blowers, generators).  
- Portable “noise fence” panels for construction sites or highway barriers.

**HOW THE ENERGY MOVES**  
Flexible piezo-ceramic or piezo-polymer sheets (or printed PVDF arrays) are laminated over a micro-perforated metamaterial absorptive layer. The metamaterial first converts chaotic pressure waves into more ordered flexural modes; the piezo layer then turns those modes into charge. A thin electromagnetic coil layer underneath catches the lower-frequency mechanical motion. Output is rectified, buffered in supercapacitors, and either:

- Fed straight into the local DC bus (data centers love this), or  
- Stored / micro-invertered for grid-tie or off-grid use.

At the same time the acoustic metamaterial and a thin active cancellation layer (driven by a fraction of the harvested power) drop the transmitted sound pressure. Net result: the machine still runs, the humans stop going deaf, and the noise itself becomes a free kilowatt-hour stream.

**DATA-CENTER SPECIALIZATION**  
Current hyperscale builds waste water on evaporative cooling and radiate a constant low-frequency drone. SonicVeil panels replace or overlay the outer acoustic treatments. The harvested electricity offsets a slice of the facility’s own parasitic load. Residual heat from the piezo and coil layers can be ducted into the existing heat-recovery loop or used to pre-warm intake air in cold climates. Water demand drops because less mechanical cooling is required once the acoustic energy is no longer pure waste heat.

**SCALING LOGIC**  
- Small: lawnmower muffler sleeve → phone-charging trickle or LED work-light power.  
- Medium: subway station canopy → lighting + ventilation assist.  
- Large: data-center facade → measurable offset of house loads and reduced water bill.

**MATERIALS BIAS**  
Favor abundant or salvage feedstock: printed piezo inks on recycled polymer, laterite-derived magnetics where possible, aluminum or steel mesh from scrap, open-cell foam from existing acoustic product waste streams. No rare-earth dependency if it can be avoided.

**STATUS**  
Pure concept node. Needs real SPL-to-power curves, fatigue life on the flexible piezo under continuous broadband excitation, and a clean way to keep the outer surface weatherproof and cleanable. The lattice already has Wattworks (human kinetic), Chronovolt (micro kinetic), and Bloomforge (living compute). SonicVeil is the missing acoustic parasite layer.

